\"connection when time is ignored\" that the task warns against.\n\n**Temporal feasibility:** a 5-hop chain with \u2264600 units per hop must complete inside ~2400 time units. But 1885 is nearly inactive (5 events, 5 partners, step_02) and 1460 likewise (4 events, step_02). Their activity barely overlaps: 1885 fires once before 18083 and then mostly after 27684 (step_06), while *all* of 1460's events occur before 27683 (step_07). Across the entire six-node candidate path, no 2400-wide sliding window contains more than 6 events total (step_16) \u2014 far too sparse to host the required strictly ordered 5-edge chain, and no window shows the concentration a real cascade burst would produce.\n\n**Confounder controls:** the global window is busy (7194 events, 1950 active nodes, step_01), and a static path does exist (steps 08\u201315) \u2014 but neither implies temporal transmission; the sliding-window scan (step_16) rules out the tight co-occurrence such a path would require.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_51debc25\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1885, 749, 1453, 1871, 632, 1460],\n  \"window\": [3683, 42083],\n  \"narrative\": \"Forward expansion from 1885 and backward expansion into 1460 meet only at node 1871, yielding a single static route 1885->749->1453->1871->632->1460 of length 5. Such a chain with a 600-unit inter-event limit must complete within ~2400 time units, but both endpoints are extremely low-activity (5 and 4 events) and their activity is temporally disjoint: 1460's inbound events all end by ~27683 while 1885's events cluster after 27684. Sliding 2400-wide windows over the whole candidate path never exceed 6 events, so no strictly ordered, gap-respecting 5-edge chain can be assembled. The apparent link is a time-ignoring artifact plus high background volume, not a genuine cascade.\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.66,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\"